  "policies": [
    "Stat-to-seconds reference curves precede second-to-second perk profiles. Multipliers do not alter reload/nocking, minimum release or damage. Only full timing consumes these profiles in the reference weapon.",
    "Full timing is sampled on accepted press. Buff expiry or later activation changes the next press, not an accepted deadline.",
    "Precision activation requires applied weapon damage excluding explosive perk damage. Both triggers require original owner, matching weapon and drawn weapon; late stowed shots cannot regrant removed buffs. These eligibility boundaries need original-game calibration.",
    "Warm-Up grants six seconds when inactive; active kills extend remaining time by four/five with a twenty-second remaining cap. Exact expiry is processed before a new kill.",
    "A drawn weapon may receive Warm-Up from its delayed Explosive Head body explosion kill; the blast never invents precision. Unusual derived-proc eligibility remains unverified.",
    "Separate multiplier families multiply. One shared Buff timer per weapon. Duplicate producer event delivery is not made idempotent by modifier-family reduction.",
    "Finite double coefficients represent the rational reference formulas. Accepted positive timing rounds upward to microseconds; algebraic rearrangement can differ at microsecond boundaries. Original frame quantization is unverified.",
    "Consumer stat50 is a chosen reference input. Minimum release .1s, body10/precision2, ammo/cadence/reload/flight and fuse remain synthetic. Partial draw keeps fixed synthetic damage; no original partial/perfect formula is asserted."
  ],
